WEBVTT

00:00:58.215 --> 00:01:00.094
than the ROVs James Cameron used

00:01:00.094 --> 00:01:03.699
to explore the Titanic.

00:01:03.699 --> 00:01:05.909
So ROVs aren't new.

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:07.617
They've been around for decades.

00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:10.653
Scientists use ROVs to explore the oceans.

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:13.472
Oil and gas companies use them for exploration

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.019
and construction.

00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:17.781
What we've built isn't unique.

00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:20.655
It's how we've built it that's really unique.

00:01:20.655 --> 00:01:23.636
So I want to give you a quick story
of how it got started.

00:01:23.636 --> 00:01:25.907
So a few years ago, my friend Eric and I

00:01:25.907 --> 00:01:28.107
decided we wanted to explore this underwater cave

00:01:28.107 --> 00:01:29.965
in the foothills of the Sierras.

00:01:29.965 --> 00:01:31.868
